After k62 an existing install moves to the new layout (agents/rules as `.local.<name>`, per-skill `.gitignore`, fixed blocks) only on the next real sync. The SessionStart hook syncs only when `check` sees a change, so a setup with only git sources keeps the old layout – and the old per-path `.gitignore` block that changes with machine state – until the next upstream change or a manual `skilletor sync`.

Fix: `check` (offline, read-only, like the existing lock-vs-targets test in spec §14.3) also reports a change when the lock does not match the current layout: an agent/rule entry (Claude, or a Codex agent) whose files lack the `.local.` prefix, or – with `gitignore` enabled – a skill entry without its `skills/<name>/.gitignore` (and the reverse with `gitignore` disabled). Spec §14.3 gets the sentence.

Done when: a lock from the 0.2.0 layout makes `check` report a change and the hook migrates in one session; a current lock does not; tests cover both harnesses and the gitignore switch; full check chain green.

